speechtext:
True, even more leeway than that gives him. I think that is explained in the note ;

If a license is to be forfeited, there is no need of advertising the fact for three months in public print and requiring that proposed executive action should be delayed for four months and then on demand refer it to the Exchequer Court for approval or non-approval.
But the minister expresses his desire of making the thing easy and getting away, from the harshness of the old statute. The only difference between us is that I want him to go a little further away from it then, perhaps, he wants to go. I do not see any injury to the public interest in making this six months instead of ninety days.
